<!--
  Every route the site wants indexed. The 404 page is deliberately absent: it
  has no real path, and listing it would invite crawlers to index an error page.

  URLs are absolute because the sitemap spec requires it — a relative path here
  is silently ignored. Kept in sync by hand, so a new route in main.jsx needs a
  matching <url> below.

  There is no <changefreq> or <priority>: Google ignores both outright. There is
  no <lastmod> either, since a hardcoded date would start lying the first time a
  page changed without someone remembering to edit it, and a wrong <lastmod> is
  treated as a reason to trust the whole file less.
-->
